{"type":"message","id":"887ea8b6","parentId":"7a4b8d7c","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:56:15.249Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the doc folder is created. Now I'll write the document with the required structure. Let me craft a friendly, simple explanation that a 10-year-old would understand, using analogies and avoiding jargon.\n\nKey elements to include:\n1. What is OpenClaw? (robot butler analogy)\n2. Main parts: Gateway (brain), Agents (helpers), Channels (how you talk), Tools (what it can do)\n3. How they work together with ASCII diagram\n4. Where stuff is saved\n5. How to teach new tricks\n6. Key words explained (spawn, session, routing)\n\nI'll aim for ~1200 words, with each section being short and sweet, using emojis and simple ASCII drawings.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create the beginner-friendly guide:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_31bbfa9d82434722844e608d","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# OpenClaw for Beginners 🤖\n\n*Imagine explaining this to a 10-year-old or your grandma who's never used a computer before!*\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is OpenClaw? (The Robot Butler Analogy) 🎩\n\n**OpenClaw is like having a SUPER-smart robot butler living inside your computer!** 🤖✨\n\nThink about it like this:\n\n- You know how in movies, billionaires have a butler named Jeeves who does EVERYTHING? He answers the door, brings you tea, schedules your meetings, finds your lost socks, and even reminds you about birthdays?\n- **OpenClaw is your computer's Jeeves!** It's not a physical robot (it won't walk around with a tray), but it's a smart program that helps you do all kinds of stuff on your computer and the internet.\n- You **talk** to OpenClaw, and it **does** things for you. Want to search the web? Write a file? Check something? Just ask your robot butler!\n\n**The cool part:** OpenClaw doesn't just do one thing. It can learn new skills, remember stuff you tell it, and work while you're doing other things. It's like having a helpful friend who's ALWAYS awake and ready to help! 🦸\n\n---\n\n## 2. The Main Parts (The Butler's Team) 👥\n\nYour robot butler has a whole team inside! Let's meet them:\n\n### 🧠 **Gateway** = The Brain\n\nThe **Gateway** is the **BOSS BRAIN** of OpenClaw. It's the control center that decides everything:\n\n- ✅ **Receives your requests** (when you say \"Hey, do this!\")\n- ✅ **Figures out who should do it** (which helper is best for the job)\n- ✅ **Keeps everything organized**\n- ✅ **Remembers your preferences** (like how you like your tea... or your files!)\n\nImagine the Gateway as the **butler's butler** — it's so smart it manages all the other helpers!\n\n---\n\n### 🧑‍🔧 **Agents** = The Helpers\n\n**Agents** are the **workers** who actually DO the jobs. They're like specialized employees in a big company:\n\n- 📧 **Email Agent**: \"I check emails all day!\"\n- 🔍 **Research Agent**: \"I search the web for answers!\"\n- 🗂️ **File Agent**: \"I organize your documents!\"\n- 💬 **Chat Agent**: \"I talk to people for you!\"\n- 🎨 **Creative Agent**: \"I write stories and make art!\"\n\nEach agent has a **specialty**. When you ask OpenClaw to do something, the Gateway picks the right agent for the job. It's like calling the right person: you don't ask the plumber to fix your computer! 🚰≠💻\n\n---\n\n### 📢 **Channels** = How You Talk\n\n**Channels** are the **phones** or **walkie-talkies** you use to talk to OpenClaw. Different channels for different places:\n\n- 💬 **Discord/Slack Channel**: You type in a chat room and OpenClaw answers there\n- 📱 **Telegram Channel**: You message OpenClaw on your phone\n- 🖥️ **Direct Console**: You type commands right on your computer\n- 🌐 **Web Chat**: You talk to OpenClaw through a website\n\nThink of channels like different **rooms** in your house. You can talk to your butler from the kitchen, living room, or bedroom — wherever you are! The butler hears you no matter which room you're in. 🏠\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 **Tools** = The Skills\n\n**Tools** are the **actual abilities** the agents use. They're like the butler's **toolbelt**:\n\n- 🔎 **Search Tool**: \"Let me Google that for you!\"\n- 📝 **Write Tool**: \"I'll type that up right away!\"\n- 📂 **Read File Tool**: \"Let me check what's in that folder...\"\n- 🌍 **Web Fetch Tool**: \"I'll grab that website for you!\"\n- 🎤 **TTS Tool**: \"I'll read it out loud!\"\n\nEach agent carries a set of tools for their job. The Research Agent has search tools, the File Agent has read/write tools, etc. When you ask something, the agent uses the right tool from their belt to get it done! 🛠️\n\n---\n\n## 3. How They All Work Together (The Magic Flow) 🔄\n\nHere's how your robot butler team works together when you ask for something:\n\n```\n    YOU\n     |\n     | (You say: \"Find info about cats!\")\n     ↓\n┌─────────────────┐\n│    CHANNEL     │ ← Where you send the message\n│  (Discord, etc) │   (your walkie-talkie)\n└────────┬────────┘\n         │\n         ↓\n┌─────────────────┐\n│    GATEWAY      │ ← The brain that receives\n│   (The Boss)    │   and decides what to do\n└────────┬────────┘\n         │\n         ↓ (routes to Research Agent)\n┌─────────────────┐\n│     AGENT       │ ← The helper with the right\n│  (Researcher)   │   skills for this job\n└────────┬────────┘\n         │\n         ↓ (uses search tool)\n┌─────────────────┐\n│     TOOL        │ ← Does the actual work\n│   (Search)      │   (like a physical tool)\n└────────┬────────┘\n         │\n         ↓\n    RESULT comes back through the same path\n```\n\n**Simple example:** You want to know \"What's the weather today?\"\n\n1. **You** → Type in Discord: \"What's the weather?\"\n2. **Channel** → Sends it to OpenClaw\n3. **Gateway** → Receives it and thinks: \"Hmm, this needs the Research Agent!\"\n4. **Agent** → The Research Agent wakes up and says: \"I'll use my Search Tool!\"\n5. **Tool** → The Search Tool goes on the internet and finds the weather\n6. **Result** → Comes back through the chain: Agent → Gateway → Channel → Discord → **You see: \"It's 75°F and sunny!\"** ☀️\n\n**All of this happens in SECONDS!** ⚡\n\n---\n\n## 4. Where Your Stuff is Saved (The Digital Filing Cabinet) 📁\n\nOpenClaw keeps all your stuff in a special folder on your computer. Think of it like a **real filing cabinet** 🗄️ in your home office:\n\n```\nD:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\workspace-osint\\\n│\n├── 📄 doc/                  ← Documentation (like this file!)\n│   └── openclaw-for-beginners.md\n│\n├── 📁 memory/               ← Daily notes (like a diary)\n│   ├── 2025-01-15.md\n│   ├── 2025-01-16.md\n│   └── ...\n│\n├── 📘 MEMORY.md             ← Long-term memories (important stuff to remember)\n│\n├── 📋 AGENTS.md             ← Who's who (about the agents)\n│\n├── 🛠️ TOOLS.md              ← What tools are available\n│\n└── 📝 HEARTBEAT.md          ← Reminders for the butler\n```\n\n**What goes where?**\n\n- **`memory/` folder**: Everyday notes — like a **diary** of what happened each day. OpenClaw reads these to remember recent conversations.\n- **`MEMORY.md`**: The **important stuff** — lessons learned, preferences, things you specifically told it to remember long-term. This is like the **highlight reel** of your relationship with OpenClaw! 🎬\n- **`doc/` folder**: All the **instructions and explanations** (like this one!). This is the **user manual**.\n- **`AGENTS.md` & `TOOLS.md`**: Information about the team members and their skills.\n\n**The best part:** YOU own all this data! It's on YOUR computer, not in some faraway cloud. You can look at it, back it up, or move it anytime. It's YOUR digital stuff! 🔐\n\n---\n\n## 5. How You Can Teach It New Tricks (The Magic of Learning) 🎓\n\nOpenClaw is **super smart**, but it's not magic — it learns from YOU! Here's how you can teach it new things:\n\n### **Method 1: Tell it what to remember** 🗣️\n\nJust say: *\"Remember that my favorite coffee is latte with oat milk!\"*\n\nOpenClaw will write that down in `MEMORY.md` and will remember it forever (or until you tell it to forget).\n\n---\n\n### **Method 2: Give it new instructions** 📜\n\nYou can add **new workflows** (fancy word for \"steps to do something\"):\n\n- \"When I say 'good morning', tell me the weather and my first appointment\"\n- \"If someone asks about Project X, send them this document\"\n- \"Every Friday, make a summary of what we did this week\"\n\nYou write these as **simple text files** or **configuration**, and OpenClaw follows them like a recipe! 📖\n\n---\n\n### **Method 3: Add new Agents or Tools** 🔨\n\nThis is for **advanced users** (like the chefs who create new recipes):\n\n- **Create a new Agent** that specializes in something (e.g., a \"Coding Agent\" that writes programs)\n- **Give it new Tools** (e.g., a \"Python Runner\" tool that executes code)\n- **Teach it new skills** by writing code and configuration\n\nIt's like **hiring a new employee** for your butler team! You write the job description (code), and OpenClaw hires them (loads them). 🧑‍💼\n\n---\n\n### **Method 4: Correct it and give feedback** 👍👎\n\nOpenClaw isn't perfect (yet!). If it does something wrong, you can say:\n\n- \"Actually, the answer was 42, not 43. Remember that.\"\n- \"Don't use that tone when talking to my boss.\"\n- \"That file should go in the 'reports' folder, not 'drafts'.\"\n\nIt learns from feedback, just like you learned not to touch the hot stove! 🔥❌\n\n---\n\n**The Magic Sauce:** OpenClaw combines **your instructions** + **its built-in abilities** + **what it already knows** = It can do MORE and MORE over time. It's like a **super-smart pet that you can train** (but it doesn't need walks)! 🐕‍🦺\n\n---\n\n## 6. Key Words Explained (The Secret Code) 🔐\n\nWhen people talk about OpenClaw, they use weird words. Here's what they **REALLY** mean:\n\n---\n\n### **\"Spawn\"** 👶\n\n**What it sounds like:** \"The spider spawned baby spiders!\" 🕷️\n\n**What it means:** \"Create a new Agent (helper) that runs independently.\"\n\n**In simple words:** Imagine your butler team. Usually, you have one butler. But sometimes you need extra help (like a party with 100 guests). You tell OpenClaw: \"Spawn 5 more chat helpers!\" and BOOM — 5 new agents appear and start working. They're like **temporary workers** you hire for a big job.\n\n**Analogy:** Spawning is like saying **\"Let there be a new helper!\"** and POOF, it exists.\n\n---\n\n### **\"Session\"** 💬\n\n**What it sounds like:** \"The tennis session is over.\" 🎾\n\n**What it means:** \"One continuous conversation or task.\"\n\n**In simple words:** A **session** is one \"chat\" or \"work period\" with OpenClaw. It starts when you first say \"hi\" and ends when you say \"bye\" (or it times out). During that session, OpenClaw remembers what you said earlier (like \"I want a sandwich\" then \"make it ham\" — it knows you're still talking about the sandwich).\n\n**Analogy:** A session is like a **phone call**. When you call your friend, that's one session. You can talk about many things during that call, but it's still ONE conversation. When you hang up, the session ends.\n\n---\n\n### **\"Routing\"** 🧭\n\n**What it sounds like:** \"The router routes internet traffic.\" 📡\n\n**What it means:** \"Figuring out where to send a message or task.\"\n\n**In simple words:** When you say \"Hey OpenClaw, do X!\", the **Gateway** (the brain) has to **route** your request to the right **Agent**. Routing is like **GPS for your message** — it finds the best path:\n\n- \"Is this about files? Send to File Agent.\"\n- \"Is this about the web? Send to Research Agent.\"\n- \"Is this a question? Send to Chat Agent.\"\n\n**Analogy:** Routing is like a **receptionist** at a big office. You tell the receptionist \"I need help with my computer,\" and they route you to the IT department, not the accounting department. The receptionist is the **Gateway**, and the IT department is the **Agent**.\n\n---\n\n### **\"Subagent\"** 🎭\n\n**What it sounds like:** A smaller agent. Like \"subway\" is a small way? Hmm…\n\n**What it means:** \"A special agent that works on ONE specific task, and it's not the main one.\"\n\n**In simple words:** Remember how I said you can **spawn** extra helpers? Those helpers are **subagents**. They're like **temp workers** or **contractors** who come in for one job and then leave. The main agent (your regular butler) might **spawn a subagent** to do a specific task while the main butler keeps helping you with other stuff.\n\n**Analogy:** Imagine you're building a treehouse. You (the main agent) are sawing wood and hammering nails. Then you need an electrician to wire the lights. You **spawn** (call) a **subagent** (the electrician). They come, do their job, and leave. You're still the main person in charge, but you got specialized help! 🔌\n\n---\n\n### **\"Heartbeat\"** 💓\n\n**What it sounds like:** Your heart going thump-thump.\n\n**What it means:** \"A regular check-in to see if everything's okay and maybe do some background work.\"\n\n**In simple words:** OpenClaw has a **heartbeat** — it's like an **alarm clock** that goes off every so often (every 30 minutes, maybe). When it rings, OpenClaw thinks:\n\n1. \"Is there anything urgent I should tell the human about?\"\n2. \"Did any emails come in?\"\n3. \"Is there a calendar event soon?\"\n4. \"Should I clean up old files?\"\n\nIt's **proactive** — it checks up on things without you asking, like a good butler should! 🎩✨\n\n---\n\n### **\"Context\"** 📚\n\n**What it sounds like:** \"Give me the context of that meeting.\"\n\n**What it means:** \"The background information that helps understand what's happening now.\"\n\n**In simple words:** **Context** is the **recent memory** of your conversation. If you say \"What's the weather?\" then \"How about tomorrow?\", OpenClaw needs to know that \"tomorrow\" refers to weather (not your birthday party). The context is the **conversation history** that everyone agrees on.\n\n**Analogy:** Context is like **the last few minutes of chat history** in a group text. If someone says \"That was funny!\", you need to know what \"that\" refers to — you scroll up and see the joke. OpenClaw keeps context so it knows what \"that\", \"it\", \"she\", etc. mean! 👀\n\n---\n\n### **\"Toolbelt\"** 🛠️\n\n**What it sounds like:** A belt that holds tools. Like Batman's belt! 🦇\n\n**What it means:** \"The set of Tools that an Agent has access to.\"\n\n**Simple words:** Each Agent carries a **toolbelt** with their favorite tools. The Research Agent's toolbelt has Search, Web Fetch, and Read tools. The File Agent's toolbelt has Write, Edit, and Delete tools. When they go to work, they pick the right tool from their belt.\n\n---\n\n### **\"Channel\"** 📺 (again, but simpler)\n\nYou already know channels are how you talk to OpenClaw. But here's another way to think about it:\n\n**A channel is like a different TV station.** 📺\n\n- Switch to **Channel 3 (Discord)** → You talk to OpenClaw through Discord\n- Switch to **Channel 5 (Telegram)** → You talk through Telegram\n- Switch to **Channel 7 (Console)** → You talk directly on the computer\n\nSame show (OpenClaw), different ways to watch it! 🎬\n\n---\n\n## 🎉 You Did It! You're Now an OpenClaw Expert! 🎓\n\nThat's it! You just learned:\n\n✅ What OpenClaw is (a robot butler for your computer)  \n✅ The 4 main parts (Gateway brain, Agents helpers, Channels talking, Tools skills)  \n✅ How they work together (the flow diagram)  \n✅ Where stuff is saved (in your computer's filing cabinet)  \n✅ How to teach it new tricks (tell it, give instructions, add new helpers)  \n✅ And all the weird words (spawn, session, routing, etc.)\n\n**Remember:** OpenClaw is YOUR helper. You're the boss! 🧑‍💼 Your robot butler is there to make your life easier, organize your stuff, and do boring tasks so YOU can do fun things.\n\nGive it a try! Start with something simple: *\"Hey OpenClaw, what's the weather today?\"* and watch the magic happen! ✨\n\n---\n\n*📝 This guide lives in:* `doc/openclaw-for-beginners.md`  \n*📖 Read it anytime you forget how things work!*\n\n🦾 **Happy Clawing!** 🦾\n","file_path":"doc/openclaw-for-beginners.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":10770,"output":4312,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15082,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771350933655}}
